From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Add an explicit override that forces HDR.

0066 stopped DXVK_HDR=1 (set by the legacy PROTON_ENABLE_HDR=1) from
overriding an SDR result for an output, because games such as Saints Row
hang on NVIDIA when HDR is reported on an output with HDR disabled
(#541). Output HDR state now comes only from the compositor's
color-management luminances: HDR is reported when the output's maximum
luminance is above its reference (SDR white) luminance.

Two setups need to override that result:

- KWin with SDR brightness set to the monitor's peak reports
  max_lum == ref_lum, which is SDR by that definition, although Plasma's
  HDR toggle is on (#838). KWin developers consider this correct, since
  there is no HDR headroom, and asked us not to read KWin's private
  kde-output-device-v2 state instead, so the patch doing that was
  dropped.
- Compositors that switch an output to HDR when a fullscreen client
  presents HDR content (e.g. Hyprland's render:cm_auto_hdr) never switch,
  since the game sees an SDR output and never requests HDR.

WAYLANDDRV_FORCE_HDR=1, set by Proton for PROTON_FORCE_HDR=1, reports
every output as HDR-enabled. DXVK_NO_HDR=1 and DXVK_HDR=0 still take
precedence. It is a separate opt-in rather than a revival of the
PROTON_ENABLE_HDR behaviour, so existing launch options keep the #541 fix.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/838

Runtime validation needed after rebuilding:
- KWin, HDR on, SDR brightness at the peak: HDR offered with the override,
  SDR without it.
- Hyprland with render:cm_auto_hdr and an SDR desktop: monitor switches
  to HDR for a fullscreen HDR game with the override.
- DXVK_NO_HDR=1 still disables HDR with the override set.
---

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/display.c
@@ -382,7 +382,10 @@
     /* We don't have a direct way to get the work area in Wayland. */
     monitor.rc_work = monitor.rc_monitor;
     monitor.hdr_enabled = output->supports_hdr;
-    /* An HDR request cannot enable HDR on an SDR compositor output. */
+    /* An HDR request cannot enable HDR on an SDR compositor output, unless
+     * the user explicitly forces it (PROTON_FORCE_HDR=1). */
+    if ((env = getenv("WAYLANDDRV_FORCE_HDR")) && *env == '1')
+        monitor.hdr_enabled = TRUE;
     if ((env = getenv("DXVK_NO_HDR")) && *env == '1')
         monitor.hdr_enabled = FALSE;
     if ((env = getenv("DXVK_HDR")) && *env == '0')
